# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# BETZ360 ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ─── SERVER-ONLY (used by Netlify functions, never bundled) ──────
# Set in: Netlify → Site Settings → Environment variables

# The Odds API — used by netlify/functions/props.js + closing-line.js
ODDS_API_KEY=your_odds_api_key_here

# OpenWeather — used by netlify/functions/weather.js
WEATHER_API_KEY=your_openweather_api_key_here

# ─── FRONTEND-SAFE (Supabase keys ARE designed to be public) ─────
# These travel with the bundle. Security is handled by Row Level
# Security policies on the Supabase database itself.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://yourprojectid.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your_supabase_anon_key_here

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SECURITY RULES
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 1. NEVER use the Supabase service_role key in this app — it has
#    admin privileges. Only the anon key is safe to expose.
# 2. NO third-party API key (besides Supabase) should start with VITE_.
# 3. Set up Row Level Security (RLS) policies — see /supabase-setup.sql
